[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Combat/Actions/ActionDefinitionResource.cs" id="2_action"]

; The first weapon to author its own chain rather than inherit the synthesised one (the 2026-09-04
; combat/animation overhaul). It is the right one to do first because it is the weapon the old
; system flattered least: under the stopwatch FSM the Iron King's two-metre maul and a dagger played
; the same Sword_Slash at the same speed, and both of its links used one set of timings.
;
; Two links, and they are genuinely different blows:
;
;   1. A LATERAL SWEEP. Interruptible, the shorter of the two, and the one that is safe to open with.
;      A well-timed stagger during its wind-up still stops it dead — the punish window this fight has
;      always had.
;   2. AN OVERHEAD SLAM. Uninterruptible: once the King commits to raising it, nothing stops it
;      landing. That is what the poise system was for and what no authored content had ever used.
;      It is slower, roots him completely (MoveScale 0), and hits for nearly twice the sweep.
;
; ⚠️ THE SLAM'S HYPERARMOR IS A REAL DIFFICULTY CHANGE, NOT A PRESENTATION ONE. It is deliberately
; paired with the longest wind-up in the game (0.62 of a 2.1 s action ≈ 1.3 s of raised maul) so the
; answer is to leave rather than to trade. Telegraph, then commitment; a boss that cannot be
; interrupted out of a fast attack would just be unfair.

